### ==============================================================================
### Enterprise Spring Boot MongoDB - REST API Verification Suite
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Create Source Account (Alice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountNumber": "ACC-ALICE-100",
  "customerId": "CUST-ALICE-01",
  "initialDeposit": 1000.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 2. Create Destination Account (Bob)
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountNumber": "ACC-BOB-200",
  "customerId": "CUST-BOB-02",
  "initialDeposit": 250.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### 3. Fetch Alice's Account
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE-100
Accept: application/json

### 4. Execute Atomic Multi-Document Transactional Transfer
# Debits ACC-ALICE-100, Credits ACC-BOB-200, creates 2 dual-entry ledger records
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccountNumber": "ACC-ALICE-100",
  "toAccountNumber": "ACC-BOB-200",
  "amount": 350.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "description": "Enterprise consulting milestone #1 payment"
}

### 5. Test Optimistic Locking Conflict Simulation
# Simulates passing a stale version (e.g. version 0 when db is version 1)
# Returns HTTP 409 CONFLICT with CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION_CONFLICT
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/ACC-ALICE-100/simulate-concurrency?amountDelta=50.00&staleVersion=0
Accept: application/json

### 6. Create Polymorphic PaymentEvent
# Stored in 'domain_events' with _class="PAYMENT" and 30-day TTL expiry
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "_type": "PAYMENT",
  "eventId": "EVT-PAY-8801",
  "aggregateId": "ACC-ALICE-100",
  "aggregateType": "ACCOUNT",
  "amount": {
    "amount": "350.00",
    "currency": "USD"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "ACH_DIRECT",
  "status": "SETTLED",
  "transactionReference": "TX-REF-100982",
  "customerId": "CUST-ALICE-01"
}

### 7. Create Polymorphic UserActivityEvent
# Stored in 'domain_events' with _class="USER_ACTIVITY"
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "_type": "USER_ACTIVITY",
  "eventId": "EVT-ACT-9902",
  "aggregateId": "ACC-ALICE-100",
  "aggregateType": "ACCOUNT",
  "userId": "USR-ALICE",
  "actionType": "TRANSFER_AUTHORIZED_MFA",
  "ipAddress": "203.0.113.195",
  "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0 Enterprise Client",
  "metadata": {
    "authMethod": "FIDO2_WEBAUTHN",
    "deviceRiskScore": "LOW"
  }
}

### 8. Fetch Polymorphic Events for Aggregate
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/aggregate/ACC-ALICE-100
Accept: application/json

### 9. Query Payment Events specifically by Customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/payments/customer/CUST-ALICE-01
Accept: application/json

### 10. Execute Complex Aggregation Pipeline
# Aggregates $match, $lookup (join with customers), $unwind, $group, $project, $sort
GET {{baseUrl}}/analytics/top-spenders?limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 11. Health & Operational Metrics (Spring Boot Actuator)
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
Accept: application/json
